  "notes": "Near-complete 0-100 from two independent sources (codingmarble and shalusharma agree on most forms; roman normalized to ASCII, diacritics stripped). Marked draft pending native review. एकोण- pattern (one short of next ten) for 19,29,...89; 99 also एकोणशंभर. Fractions: deed=1.5, adheech=2.5 (अडीच), savva=1.25 (सव्वा, e.g. सव्वाशे = 125), pavne/paun = 3/4 of next unit (e.g. पावणे दोनशे = 175), sade = +1/2 (साडेतीनशे = 350). Decimalization of fractions is identical to Hindi usage."
